We at EY-Parthenon, a strategic management consultancy hand of EY, are committed to bringing unconventional yet pragmatic thinking together with our clients’ smarts to deliver actionable strategies for real impact in today’s complex business landscape. We develop outstanding leaders who team up to deliver on our promises to all of our stakeholders. In doing so, we play a critical role in building a better working world for our clients, our people and our communities.
As a top tier management consulting company, we serve our clients in multiple industries across multiple project topics, such as Strategy & Growth, Value Creation, Commercial Due Diligence, PMI and many more.
We offer our employees a dynamic working environment with exposure to top-notch regional and international clients and ability to address their strategic challenges and ambitions, while working in a diverse team with great culture and spirit.
Your key responsibilities
As Senior in Corporate Strategy, at EY Parthenon, your will have the following responsibilities:
- Lead client projects and engagement teams to deliver high quality outputs;
- Maintain relationships with client personnel at appropriate levels;
- Drive business development by preparing client meetings and project proposals and proactively seeking and identifying new project opportunities;
- Demonstrate advanced knowledge of all phases and aspects of strategy development and implementation;
- Deliver a high degree of client satisfaction with the engagement process and work products sufficient to drive additional and repeated engagements;
- Develop business strategies using tools such as market analysis, customer research, portfolio optimization, etc;
- Effectively manage diverse and international teams, maintaining the work life balance and promoting EY-Parthenon culture and values;
- Mentor and coach junior colleagues to support their personal and professional growth and fit to the team;
- Lead marketing and promotional efforts to further boost brand presence and awareness;
- Actively support recruitment efforts in identifying and selecting future team members.
Skills and attributes for success
- Able to independently lead projects & teams and manage senior-level clients;
- Highly motivated with positive, “can-do” attitude;
- Team player, capable to effectively operate and communicate in an international, multicultural and diverse environment;
- Strong business acumen and communication skills;
- Proactive and willing to handle several complex tasks simultaneously;
- Outstanding organizational skills, flexibility and ability to work under tight deadlines;
- International exposure and experience (professional and/or educational);
- Capable to effectively contribute and lead business development activities.
To qualify for the role, you must have
- Academic bachelor or master;
- 3-5 years of experience, including in strategic consulting;
- Project management skills: Delivery structure and conclusions, completion of demanding plans, management and coordination of team members and management of the relationship with the client and heads of other departments;
- Commercial skills to identify new customers and opportunities;
- Full Portuguese and English Proficiency.
What we offer you
At EY, we’ll develop you with future-focused skills and equip you with world-class experiences. We’ll empower you in a flexible environment, and fuel you and your extraordinary talents in a diverse and inclusive culture of globally connected teams. Learn more.
Are you ready to shape your future with confidence? Apply today.

Job Description & Summary
Are you intrigued by operating models and eager to improve operational efficiency in an M&A environment? Do you want to apply your analytical mindset on high-impact deals for leading Private Equity clients? Join our Delivering Deal Value (DDV) team within PwC's Deals practice — the most successful deals practice in the Netherlands. You'll work on operational due diligence and value creation projects for corporate and private equity clients, in a diverse and international team. You'll gain direct exposure to top-tier PE clients, a global network, and challenging projects where your recommendations directly impact deal outcomes.
This is what you'll do
You'll be part of an inclusive, experienced advisory team that supports corporate and private equity firms in identifying, quantifying and delivering full deal value — with greater speed, insight and confidence. You'll work on challenging client assignments in both pre- and post-deal phases, using the latest technology including AI-tools, and grow in an environment where coaching and personal development are central.
Our approach combines industry experience with data analytics and practical sector knowledge. Projects typically start early in the deal cycle and deliver concrete operational upsides that directly influence the deal offer. In your role, you will:
-
Identify operational gaps at leading businesses and provide recommendations that drive value creation;
-
Develop implementation plans and quantify savings using a driver-based approach and industry benchmarking data;
-
Drive transformation initiatives with a focus on short- and long-term value realization;
-
Manage client relationships at both executive and operational level throughout all project phases;
-
Contribute to our core services: Operational Due Diligence, Pre-deal Value Creation, and Carve-out support.
You recognize yourself in this
You are analytical, commercially minded and enjoy working closely with clients and colleagues in a dynamic deal environment. You communicate clearly, take initiative, and know how to motivate people around you to deliver high-quality advice.
-
At least 4 years of relevant experience in (deals) consulting, operational performance improvement, corporate M&A teams, COO support roles or specialized operations consulting;
-
A university degree in Business Administration, Science, Finance, Engineering or a related discipline;
-
Solid understanding of one or more core operational functions (e.g. Finance, Supply Chain, Working Capital, Procurement, Sales);
-
Comfortable working with and interpreting financial information;
-
Fluent in English, both written and spoken; professional level of Dutch is highly appreciated.
What we offer
With us, you’ll have the chance to be yourself, perform at your best in a high-performance organization, and grow within our global network. We offer you, among other things:
-
A competitive salary based on your experience, an annual bonus (depending on results and personal development), and the opportunity to grow;
-
A motivating work environment where collaboration with ambitious colleagues and recognition for your contributions are central;
-
A wide range of tailored training via our AI-based Growth Center, linked to skills and goals and focused on professional growth and leadership development;
-
Choose the mobility option that suits you best: an electric lease car or a mobility allowance for your business travel costs, plus access to various mobility providers via one convenient app;
-
29 vacation days and the option to purchase additional days;
-
At PwC, your well-being is our priority. That’s why we offer a personal well-being budget to help you grow in physical and mental health, as well as access to the well-being platform OpenUp;
-
You’ll work on challenging and meaningful client projects, use cutting-edge technology such as AI-tools, learn from the best, and receive support through coaching. Together, we work as an inclusive team to make a real impact;
-
You work at client locations and our office, with flexibility for hybrid working where possible;
-
A monthly net expense allowance for internet and other costs;
-
YoungPwC: You’ll have the chance to network and exchange knowledge. The experience and tips from colleagues will greatly benefit you as a young PwC professional and help you achieve your ambitions;
-
Possibility to participate in projects of communities such as I&D, art initiatives, Giving Back etc;
-
Fun extras such as various informal company and team activities.
These are just a handful of our terms of employment. Find more information on our website.
Getting started at PwC
Are you interested in this vacancy? Then let us know what motivates you and fill in your details. After we’ve received your application,
-
You’ll immediately receive confirmation in your inbox;
-
If your qualifications match the profile that we have in mind, then we’ll contact you within two weeks;
-
If everyone is enthusiastic, we’ll schedule an online assessment. Depending on the result, you'll receive an invitation for an initial interview. Click here for more information about the application process.
